WEBVTT

00:01:57.419 --> 00:02:01.719
I just couldn't figure out
how to put the love down.

00:02:03.494 --> 00:02:05.259
Then, drinking white wine one night,

00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:08.730
I saw a TED Talk by a woman
named Dr. Helen Fisher,

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:13.672
and she said that in her work, she'd
been able to map the coordinates of love

00:02:13.696 --> 00:02:14.888
in the human brain.

00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:18.653
And I thought, well,
if I could find my love in my brain,

00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:20.124
maybe I could get it out.

00:02:20.148 --> 00:02:21.538
So I went to Twitter.

00:02:22.231 --> 00:02:24.351
"Anybody got access to an fMRI lab,

00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:25.854
like at midnight or something?

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:28.394
I'll trade for backstage
passes and whiskey."

00:02:28.418 --> 00:02:30.011
(Laughter)